From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:34:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 105/107] drm/meson: add T7 VPU support

T7 uses the S4 register layout with these differences:
- VIU to VENC mux and VPU_HDMI_SETTING bits for ENC0
- HDMI PLL values and the vid_pll, ENC0 and HDMI clock dividers
- OSD1 reads by linear address; blend source 4 selects OSD1
- the VPP blends in RGB: OSD1 RGB to YUV matrix off, RGB background
- the OSD1 scaler registers moved to 0x5a00
- the secure firmware selects the encoder of HDMI: select ENC0
- the VPU interrupt gate is a clock, held by the driver
- the S4 modes plus 2160p up to 60 Hz

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
